<title>USA: Oak Industries sells unit, to take Q4 gain.</title>
<headline>Oak Industries sells unit, to take Q4 gain.</headline>
<dateline>WALTHAM, Mass. 1996-10-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Oak Industries Inc said Wednesday it has sold its Nordco unit for about $21 million, which will lead it to report a gain in this year's fourth quarter.</p>
<p>The company did not disclose the size of the gain and did not immediately return a telephone call.</p>
<p>Nordco, a railroad maintenance-equipment business, was sold to an affiliate of Milwaukee-based Banc One Venture Corp and members of Nordco management.</p>
<p>Oak Industries supplies components to manufacturers and service providers in the communications industry.</p>
</text>
